#
# ── What PASSED (the real proof) ──
# TEST 1  e2ee_text_roundtrip_between_two_accounts = ok.
#   Alice and Bob each did a real password login (fresh in-memory device:
#   alice YBIABEXLRT, bob PHXUWTIWVA), synced to upload device/one-time keys.
#   Alice created a PRIVATE + is_direct + m.room.encryption room through the
#   crate's only room-creation path (create_encrypted_dm), Bob joined, both
#   sides classified it SecurityTier::InternalE2ee. Alice sent through the
#   tier-gated send_text; the SDK queried Bob's device keys, claimed a one-time
#   key, Olm-encrypted the Megolm room key to Bob's device (m.room_key), and
#   Megolm-encrypted the event. Bob synced, decrypted it, and the delivered
#   ReceivedText carried was_encrypted=true, tier=InternalE2ee, body intact.
#   That is a genuine end-to-end live Matrix E2EE round-trip: login → sync →
#   encrypted room → Olm key share → Megolm send → sync → decrypted receive.
#
# TEST 2  session_restore_resumes_same_device_and_megolm_state = ok.
#   Alice logged in via login_password_persistent into a sqlite store
#   (device DHYJYXYAXV), snapshotted the session, and did one E2EE round-trip
#   each way (both was_encrypted=true). The client was then DROPPED ("process
#   restart") and rebuilt with MatrixMessenger::restore from the SavedSession +
#   the same sqlite store path. The core assertion held live:
#     original_device=DHYJYXYAXV  post_restore_device=DHYJYXYAXV  same=true
#   — restore resumed the SAME Matrix device (no fresh device keys). The sharp
#   edge then decrypted: a post-restart B->A message sent on Bob's PRE-restart
#   outbound Megolm session (same device_id, key already shared, so Bob did NOT
#   re-send it) arrived was_encrypted=true — which is only possible if Alice's
#   INBOUND Megolm session genuinely survived on disk across the restart, not a
#   fresh key share papering over a wiped store. A->B after restart also still
#   went out tier-gated and encrypted. This is the first live execution of the
#   persistence slice; the file header's "HONEST STATUS: restore path UNPROVEN
#   until someone runs this" is now discharged.
#
# ── Scope of this proof (the honest ceiling) ──
# Plumbing + the classical Megolm/Olm E2EE path + sqlite persistence/restore
# are proven live. Nothing more. No Tor (metadata exposed as documented), no
# post-quantum transport crypto, no device verification/cross-signing, and the
# whole crate remains a pre-release, UNAUDITED library slice — not a functional
# messenger product. The honest-limits header above holds verbatim.
